text:
The beggars on the street are not all alike. Some of them I know to be true,
And some perhaps only in fancy go out to beg their bread;
For when a man's worn-out with his labour he must have something said;
A man is weary long before he has earned what one would give.

But there are others who beg honestly enough, I dare say,
Who do no work at all through the day, but live by begging every way;
And these are not so very cheerful as those that call themselves Poor;
